# ── Videos are committed ──────────────────────────────────────
# They used to be ignored and served from a GitHub release, but
# GitHub labels release assets application/octet-stream and Safari
# refuses to play media with that content type. Vercel serves files
# from the repo as video/mp4, which iPhones are happy with.
#
# Keep an eye on size: GitHub hard-rejects any single file over
# 100MB and warns above 50MB. Git also keeps every version of a
# binary forever, so re-exporting a film adds another full copy to
# history rather than replacing the old one.
#
# If the library outgrows this, Cloudflare R2 is the next step:
# correct content types, and egress is free.

